            "url": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:wlwlvnq25nzwvz43crqo7apu/bafkreicg5g5qesui2lfpocglibetinethiscwguzlzwf6edxay4np3wnui",
            "alt": "Screenshot of a LinkedIn post, which attaches a link to an academic paper. \n\nThe post reads: “Liberals and conservatives behave differently in everyday life--conservatives seem to be out with others a lot more while liberals stay home and doomscroll. This study analyzed activity using smartphones to track college students and found that conservatives were more likely to be at parties, noisy places, fraternities and religious facilities. Liberals were at home, resting, doing chores, and browsing social media. This helps explain why conservatives are, on average, happier than liberals. The behavioral differences were small but robust, not accounted for by other plausible factors (e.g., demographics), and most pronounced in the leisure domain.”"
          }
        ]
      },
